{
  "_readme": "When each page last changed, keyed by a hash of its source. Seeded once from git history and maintained by the build: a file whose hash moved gets today, a file whose hash did not keeps its date. Git cannot do this job directly, because a date read from git history changes the moment the file is committed, so a sitemap built before the commit would never match the one rebuilt after it.",
